HST Office: Writer's Columns button puts the selection in columns, like Word

The Columns popup of the ribbon and of the sidebar (One, Two, Three, Left, Right;
SID_ATTR_PAGE_COLUMN) always changed the columns of the current page style, so putting one
paragraph in two columns put the whole document in two columns. It now works like Word:

- with a selection, a new section with the columns goes around the selection (as Format Columns
  with "Apply to: Selection" does); DOCX saves it as continuous section breaks;
- with the cursor in a section with columns, that section changes. "One" removes a section that
  does nothing but lay out columns (plain, unprotected, visible, unconditional, only column
  attributes) and keeps its text; any other section stays with one column;
- otherwise the page style changes, as before.
Left and Right keep the 2:1 column widths the page style used. New columns get Word's spacing of
1.27 cm (720 twips) instead of none; columns that already have a spacing keep it. Each click is
one undo step. The popup and the sidebar show the columns of the section around the cursor.
"More Options" in the popup opens Format Columns (with "Apply to") instead of the page style
dialog, which stays the fallback where Format Columns is disabled.

Test: CppunitTest_sw_uibase_uiview, testPageColumnType*.

